<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Canary {{ manifest.kind }} {{ manifest.run_id }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfbfa; --fg: #1d1d1b; --muted: #6b6b66; --line: #e3e2de; --card: #ffffff;
    --bad: #b42318; --bad-bg: #fdecea; --good: #1a7f37; --good-bg: #e7f5ec;
    --warn: #8a5a00; --warn-bg: #fff4d6; --accent: #3056d3;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #151514; --fg: #ecebe7; --muted: #a09f99; --line: #2e2d2a; --card: #1d1c1a;
      --bad: #ff8a80; --bad-bg: #3a1714; --good: #7ee2a0; --good-bg: #13301e;
      --warn: #f5c451; --warn-bg: #3a2c0b; --accent: #8fa8ff;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; background: var(--bg); color: var(--fg);
         font: 15px/1.5 ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; }
  main { max-width: 1080px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 32px 16px 64px; }
  h1 { font-size: 22px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  h2 { font-size: 17px; margin: 36px 0 12px; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  code, .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; font-size: 13px; }
  .card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; }
  .banner { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .badge { font-weight: 650; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 14px; }
  .regression { color: var(--bad); background: var(--bad-bg); }
  .improvement { color: var(--good); background: var(--good-bg); }
  .inconclusive { color: var(--warn); background: var(--warn-bg); }
  .kv { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 10px 20px; margin-top: 14px; }
  .kv div span { display: block; font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 7px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); vertical-align: top; }
  th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .pass { color: var(--good); font-weight: 600; }
  .fail { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 600; }
  .error { color: var(--warn); font-weight: 600; }
  .flag { color: var(--bad); font-weight: 600; }
  details { margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--accent); }
  .step { border-left: 3px solid var(--line); padding: 4px 10px; margin: 6px 0; }
  .step.agent { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .step pre { white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; margin: 4px 0; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .notes li { margin: 4px 0; }
  svg text { fill: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <h1>{{ manifest.suite_name }}: {{ "compare" if manifest.kind == "compare" else "run" }}
    {% if manifest.kind == "compare" %}<span class="mono">{{ manifest.baseline }}</span> → <span class="mono">{{ manifest.candidate }}</span>{% endif %}
  </h1>
  <div class="muted mono">{{ manifest.run_id }} · {{ manifest.created_at.strftime("%Y-%m-%d %H:%M UTC") }}
    · canary {{ manifest.canary_version }} · runner {{ manifest.runner.kind }}{% if manifest.runner.harbor_version %} (Harbor {{ manifest.runner.harbor_version }}){% endif %}
    · suite commit {{ (manifest.suite_commit or "n/a")[:10] }}{% if manifest.suite_dirty %} (dirty){% endif %}
    {% if manifest.continues %}· continues run {{ manifest.continues }} (its trials count in the verdict; they are listed in that run's report){% endif %}</div>

  {% if verdict %}
  <h2>Verdict</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="banner">
      <span class="badge {{ verdict.decision }}">
        {% if verdict.decision == "regression" %}Regression detected{% elif verdict.decision == "improvement" %}Improvement detected{% else %}Inconclusive at this budget{% endif %}
      </span>
      <span class="muted">stopped: {{ {"significant": "significant result", "budget_usd": "dollar budget reached", "max_batches": "batch limit reached", "futility": "futility look: the candidate was not behind by enough", "dead_batch": "a batch produced no usable pairs", "ledger": "campaign ledger limit reached"}[verdict.stop_reason] }}
        after {{ verdict.batches_run }} batch{{ "es" if verdict.batches_run != 1 }}</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kv">
      <div><span>E-value (threshold {{ "%g"|format(1 / verdict.alpha) }})</span>{{ "%.3g"|format(verdict.e_value) }}</div>
      <div><span>Anytime-valid p</span>{{ "%.3g"|format(verdict.p_value) }}</div>
      <div><span>Alternative</span>{{ {"less": "candidate worse", "greater": "candidate better", "two-sided": "either direction"}[verdict.alternative] }}</div>
      <div><span>{{ verdict.baseline.pin }} pass rate</span>{{ verdict.baseline.passes }}/{{ verdict.baseline.n }}{% if verdict.baseline.n %} ({{ "%.0f"|format(100 * verdict.baseline.passes / verdict.baseline.n) }}%){% endif %}</div>
      <div><span>{{ verdict.candidate.pin }} pass rate</span>{{ verdict.candidate.passes }}/{{ verdict.candidate.n }}{% if verdict.candidate.n %} ({{ "%.0f"|format(100 * verdict.candidate.passes / verdict.candidate.n) }}%){% endif %}</div>
      <div><span>Discordant pairs (regress / improve)</span>{{ verdict.n_discordant }} ({{ verdict.n_regress }} / {{ verdict.n_improve }})</div>
      <div><span>Pairs used / dropped</span>{{ verdict.n_pairs }} / {{ verdict.dropped_pairs }}</div>
      {% if verdict.baseline.checked or verdict.candidate.checked %}
      <div><span>False success / "tests pass" claims</span>{{ verdict.baseline.pin }} {{ verdict.baseline.false_success }}/{{ verdict.baseline.claims }} · {{ verdict.candidate.pin }} {{ verdict.candidate.false_success }}/{{ verdict.candidate.claims }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if verdict.baseline.cap_hits or verdict.candidate.cap_hits %}
      <div><span>Trials stopped by a spend or turn cap</span>{{ verdict.baseline.pin }} {{ verdict.baseline.cap_hits }} · {{ verdict.candidate.pin }} {{ verdict.candidate.cap_hits }}</div>
      {% endif %}
      <div><span>Spend (higher of reported and re-priced)</span>{% if not verdict.cost_known and verdict.spent_usd %}≤ {% endif %}${{ "%.2f"|format(verdict.spent_usd) }}{% if not verdict.cost_known %} <span class="error" title="Some trials had no cost and are counted at their spending cap, or at zero if they have none.">upper bound</span>{% endif %}</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if chart %}
  <h2>Evidence over batches</h2>
  <div class="card scroll">
    <svg width="{{ chart.width }}" height="{{ chart.height }}" role="img" aria-label="log10 E-value by batch">
      <line x1="{{ chart.pad }}" x2="{{ chart.width - chart.pad }}" y1="{{ chart.threshold_y }}" y2="{{ chart.threshold_y }}" stroke="currentColor" stroke-dasharray="4 4" opacity=".55"/>
      <text x="{{ chart.width - chart.pad }}" y="{{ chart.threshold_y - 6 }}" text-anchor="end">{{ chart.threshold_label }}</text>
      <line x1="{{ chart.pad }}" x2="{{ chart.width - chart.pad }}" y1="{{ chart.zero_y }}" y2="{{ chart.zero_y }}" stroke="currentColor" opacity=".2"/>
      <text x="{{ chart.pad }}" y="{{ chart.zero_y - 6 }}">E = 1</text>
      <polyline points="{{ chart.points }}" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/>
      {% for cx, cy, b in chart.dots %}<circle cx="{{ cx }}" cy="{{ cy }}" r="3.5" fill="var(--accent)"><title>batch {{ b }}</title></circle>
      <text x="{{ cx }}" y="{{ chart.height - 8 }}" text-anchor="middle">{{ b }}</text>{% endfor %}
    </svg>
    <div class="muted">log₁₀ E after each batch. Crossing the dashed line is a significant result at α = {{ verdict.alpha }}, valid despite checking after every batch (ADR-0003).</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if verdict.metrics %}
  <h2>Cost, tokens and latency</h2>
  <div class="card scroll">
    <table>
      <tr><th>Metric</th><th class="num">{{ verdict.baseline.pin }}</th><th class="num">{{ verdict.candidate.pin }}</th><th class="num">Ratio</th><th class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(100 * manifest.settings.stats.confidence) }}% CI</th><th></th></tr>
      {% for m in verdict.metrics %}
      <tr>
        <td>{{ m.metric }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "{:,.4g}".format(m.baseline_mean) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "{:,.4g}".format(m.candidate_mean) }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(m.ratio) }}×</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(m.ci_low) }}–{{ "%.3f"|format(m.ci_high) }}</td>
        <td>{% if m.flagged %}<span class="flag">increase</span>{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
    <div class="muted">{% if verdict.metrics_from_batch %}Batches before {{ verdict.metrics_from_batch }} are left out as prompt-cache warm-up. {% endif %}Means per trial; cluster bootstrap over tasks. input_tokens counts everything sent, including cache reads and writes. These intervals are fixed-sample at the stopping time, not anytime-valid.</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Per task</h2>
  <div class="card scroll">
    <table>
      <tr><th>Task</th><th class="num">{{ verdict.baseline.pin }}</th><th class="num">{{ verdict.candidate.pin }}</th><th class="num">Regressed pairs</th><th class="num">Improved pairs</th></tr>
      {% for t in verdict.per_task %}
      <tr><td><a href="#task-{{ t.task }}">{{ t.task }}</a></td>
        <td class="num">{{ t.baseline_passes }}/{{ t.baseline_n }}</td><td class="num">{{ t.candidate_passes }}/{{ t.candidate_n }}</td>
        <td class="num">{% if t.n_regress %}<span class="fail">{{ t.n_regress }}</span>{% else %}0{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{% if t.n_improve %}<span class="pass">{{ t.n_improve }}</span>{% else %}0{% endif %}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
    <div class="muted">Tasks with no discordant pairs add cost but no evidence; consider pruning ones that always pass or always fail.</div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Pins</h2>
  <div class="card scroll">
    <table>
      <tr><th>Pin</th><th>Harness</th><th>Version</th><th>Model</th><th>Options / env</th><th>Fingerprint</th></tr>
      {% for p in manifest.pins %}
      <tr><td class="mono">{{ p.name }}</td><td>{{ p.spec.harness }}</td><td class="mono">{{ p.spec.version or "—" }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ p.spec.model or "—" }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{% for k, v in p.spec.options.items() %}{{ k }}={{ v }}<br>{% endfor %}{% for k, v in p.spec.env.items() %}${{ k }}={{ v }}<br>{% endfor %}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ p.fingerprint[:12] }}</td></tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Trials ({{ n_trials }})</h2>
  {% for task, rows in by_task.items() %}
  <div class="card scroll" id="task-{{ task }}" style="margin-bottom:14px">
    <strong>{{ task }}</strong>
    <table>
      <tr><th>Batch</th><th>Pin</th><th>Status</th><th class="num">In tok</th><th class="num">Out tok</th><th class="num">Cost</th><th class="num">Agent s</th><th>Version</th><th>Claim check</th><th>Files</th></tr>
      {% for row in rows %}{% set r = row.r %}
      <tr>
        <td class="num">{{ r.batch }}</td><td class="mono">{{ r.pin }}</td>
        <td class="{{ r.status.value }}">{{ r.status.value }}{% if r.exception_type %} <span class="muted">({{ r.exception_type }})</span>{% endif %}{% if r.harness_stop and r.harness_stop != "success" %} <span class="error">{{ r.harness_stop }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(r.n_input_tokens) if r.n_input_tokens is not none else "—" }}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "{:,}".format(r.n_output_tokens) if r.n_output_tokens is not none else "—" }}</td>
        <td class="num">{% if r.cost_usd is not none %}<span title="re-priced from tokens; harness reported {{ "$%.4f"|format(r.reported_cost_usd) if r.reported_cost_usd is not none else "nothing" }}">{{ "$%.3f"|format(r.cost_usd) }}</span>{% elif r.reported_cost_usd is not none %}<span class="muted" title="harness-reported; not re-priced">{{ "$%.3f"|format(r.reported_cost_usd) }}*</span>{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
        <td class="num">{{ "%.0f"|format(r.agent_seconds) if r.agent_seconds is not none else "—" }}</td>
        <td class="mono">{{ r.installed_version or "—" }}</td>
        <td>{% set c = r.claim_check %}{% if not c or c.verdict == "no_claim" %}<span class="muted">{{ "no claim" if c else "—" }}</span>
            {% elif c.verdict == "supported" %}<span class="pass">supported</span>
            {% elif c.verdict == "false_success" %}<span class="fail" title="{{ c.claim_excerpt }}">false success</span> <span class="muted">({{ c.reason.replace("_", " ") }})</span>
            {% else %}<span class="error" title="{{ c.claim_excerpt }}">unverifiable</span>{% endif %}</td>
        <td>{% if row.result_link %}<a href="{{ row.result_link }}">result</a>{% endif %}
            {% if row.agent_link %} · <a href="{{ row.agent_link }}">agent</a>{% endif %}
            {% if row.verifier_link %} · <a href="{{ row.verifier_link }}">verifier</a>{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      {% if row.transcript or r.exception_message %}
      <tr><td></td><td colspan="9">
        {% if r.exception_message %}<details><summary>exception</summary><pre class="mono">{{ r.exception_message }}</pre></details>{% endif %}
        {% if row.transcript %}
        <details><summary>transcript ({{ row.transcript|length }} steps)</summary>
          {% for s in row.transcript %}
          <div class="step {{ s.source }}"><span class="muted mono">#{{ s.id }} {{ s.source }}</span>
            {% if s.message %}<pre>{{ s.message }}</pre>{% endif %}
            {% for c in s.calls %}<pre class="mono">→ {{ c.name }} {{ c.args }}</pre>{% endfor %}
            {% for o in s.results %}<pre class="mono muted">← {{ o }}</pre>{% endfor %}
          </div>
          {% endfor %}
        </details>
        {% endif %}
      </td></tr>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </table>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}

  <h2>Read this before acting on the numbers</h2>
  <ul class="notes muted">
    <li>The harness under test is the harness as launched by the runner{% if manifest.runner.harbor_version %} (Harbor {{ manifest.runner.harbor_version }}: headless print mode, permissions bypassed){% endif %}, not an interactive developer setup.</li>
    <li><code>cost_usd</code> is re-priced from each trial's token usage with the canary's own price table{% if manifest.settings.pricing %} (version {{ manifest.settings.pricing.version }}){% endif %}, so it does not move when a harness changes its bundled prices. If a trial cannot be re-priced, the comparison falls back to <code>reported_cost_usd</code>, the harness's own estimate, marked * in the trial tables (ADR-0005).</li>
    <li>Prompt-cache state changes cost: a trial that finds a warm cache pays cheap cache reads, a cold one pays cache writes. Compare <code>cache_write_tokens</code> between arms before reading a cost ratio as a harness effect.</li>
    <li>The pass-rate test controls false alarms under the null "average pass rate not lower", evaluated at batch boundaries. Dropped pairs are assumed unrelated to outcomes.</li>
    <li>Claim check: a rule-based reading of each transcript, with no model involved. "False success" means the agent said its tests pass, but its last test run after its last edit is missing or shows failures. It judges the agent's own claim, not the hidden tests, and it misses claims it cannot parse (ADR-0007).</li>
    <li>A trial the harness stopped at its spend or turn cap is scored by the hidden tests on whatever it had finished, which is usually a failure. If one arm hits a cap more often, the cap is part of what is being compared.</li>
    <li>Bundle integrity: <code>canary verify {{ manifest.run_id }}</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</main>
</body>
</html>
